# Security headers, served by Cloudflare Pages (this file is the live source of truth).
# The daily production smoke check compares the deployed CSP against this file
# directive by directive, so an edit here is a deployment contract change.
#
# NOTE: 'unsafe-inline' in script-src is an accepted limitation, not a proof of safety.
# next-themes and Next.js emit inline bootstrap scripts, and a static export has no
# server to issue per-request nonces; per-build script hashing is the alternative and
# is brittle across builds. So the risk is accepted rather than eliminated.
#
# Being static and form-free shrinks the request-time attack surface but does not make
# injection impossible: the build still bakes in external GitHub metadata and the page
# loads a third-party analytics script. An external grade measures header presence, not
# the absence of a vector, so it is not a justification. base-uri, object-src, and
# form-action are set below to close the sinks that 'unsafe-inline' would otherwise
# leave reachable; no <form>, <base>, <object>, or <embed> exists in any built route.
/*
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: on
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'none'
